Backend: SDD

Purpose:
  Backend technology catalog with framework options, compatibility rules,
  and selection criteria. Root stack/ defines reusable backend knowledge;
  projects/vkard.az/stack/ stores the selected backend for the current project.

Catalog:
  Go:
    net/http:
      Type: Standard Library
      Pros:
        - No external dependencies
        - Minimal footprint
        - Battle-tested
      Cons:
        - Less feature-rich than frameworks
        - Manual routing setup
      BestFor:
        - Simple services
        - Minimalist architectures
      AvoidWhen:
        - Complex middleware needs
    Gin:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Fast performance
        - Middleware ecosystem
        - Simple API
      Cons:
        - Less opinionated
        - Manual validation
      BestFor:
        - REST APIs
        - Microservices
      AvoidWhen:
        - Full-stack needs
    Echo:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - High performance
        - Extensible
        - Good middleware
      Cons:
        - Smaller ecosystem than Gin
      BestFor:
        - High-performance APIs
      AvoidWhen:
        - Complex routing needs
    Fiber:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Express.js-like API
        - High performance
        - Rapid development
      Cons:
        - Newer framework
        - Smaller community
      BestFor:
        - Express.js migrants
        - Rapid prototyping
      AvoidWhen:
        - Production-critical without review

  Java:
    Spring Boot:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Mature ecosystem
        - Excellent enterprise support
        - Auto-configuration
      Cons:
        - High operational complexity
        - Memory-heavy
      BestFor:
        - Enterprise services
        - Complex business logic
      AvoidWhen:
        - Small teams
        - Simple services

  CSharp:
    ASP.NET Core:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Excellent performance
        - Strong tooling
        - Cross-platform
      Cons:
        - Ecosystem smaller than Spring
      BestFor:
        - Enterprise services
        - Azure deployments
      AvoidWhen:
        - Linux-only without .NET experience

  PHP:
    Laravel:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Rapid development
        - Elegant syntax
        - Large ecosystem
      Cons:
        - Performance overhead
        - Magic behavior
      BestFor:
        - CRUD applications
        - Rapid prototyping
        - Content management
      AvoidWhen:
        - High-concurrency services
    Symfony:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Mature and stable
        - Enterprise-ready
        - Reusable bundles
      Cons:
        - Steeper learning curve
        - More verbose
      BestFor:
        - Enterprise PHP
        - Long-term maintenance
      AvoidWhen:
        - Rapid prototyping

  Python:
    FastAPI:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Fast development
        - Automatic OpenAPI docs
        - Type hints
      Cons:
        - Newer framework
        - Smaller ecosystem
      BestFor:
        - ML/AI APIs
        - Rapid prototyping
      AvoidWhen:
        - High-throughput services
    Django:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Batteries included
        - ORM built-in
        - Admin interface
      Cons:
        - Monolithic
        - Performance overhead
      BestFor:
        - Content-driven apps
        - Admin-heavy systems
      AvoidWhen:
        - Microservices

  Node.js:
    Express:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - Minimalist
        - Large ecosystem
        - JavaScript everywhere
      Cons:
        - Callback hell (mitigated with async/await)
        - Less opinionated
      BestFor:
        - I/O-bound services
        - Real-time applications
      AvoidWhen:
        - CPU-intensive tasks
    NestJS:
      Type: Framework
      Pros:
        - TypeScript-first
        - Opinionated architecture
        - Decorator-based
      Cons:
        - Steeper learning curve
        - More boilerplate
      BestFor:
        - Enterprise Node.js
        - Complex APIs
      AvoidWhen:
        - Simple services

SelectionRules:
  - RequirementFit: architecture requirements drive selection
  - TeamFit: existing team expertise MUST be considered
  - Ecosystem: library maturity and community support
  - Performance: latency and throughput requirements
  - Security: language/framework security track record
  - OperationalCost: hosting, monitoring, debugging complexity
  - Maintainability: long-term maintenance burden
  - Compatibility: integration with existing stack components

TechnologyScore:
  RequirementFit: 0-25
  ArchitectureFit: 0-20
  TeamFit: 0-15
  Ecosystem: 0-10
  Performance: 0-10
  Security: 0-10
  OperationalFit: 0-5
  Cost: 0-3
  Maintainability: 0-2

State: +
  